        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T08:05:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For consistency with other flags, and better rollback safety, it would be better to have CONFIG_ACTIVELY_PREFER_BAD_WIFI_VERSION which would be the minimum version number to enable the feature; and read it with DeviceConfigUtils.isFeatureEnabled\n\nHere you could use `isFeatureEnabled(namespace, flag, isAtLeastU() || configActivelyPrefersBadWifi)` to get the same behavior (default-enable the feature if U+ or enabled via overlay)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "df5d20e0f167514b3a552260e8cf39de415d248f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "183473fa_a97201f2",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/MultinetworkPolicyTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 72,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T09:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After a long discussion in person, we decided this wasn\u0027t very appropriate for this device config, as it\u0027s a tri-state (force off/force on/unset), and it only ships on S+ meaning rollback protection is enforced by device config anyway. We could achieve this by having two different flags (one for force on and one for force off) but the complexity that comes with this doesn\u0027t sound like time very well spent.\n\nAgreed to have a comment in the code to tell possible future developers that this scheme is not what you need for features.",
      "parentUuid": "6f745f7c_e273c6a2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 72,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 72,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "df5d20e0f167514b3a552260e8cf39de415d248f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
