      "writtenOn": "2022-09-26T08:05:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not introduced here, but I find the naming very non-explicit; it may be difficult to explain to OEMs when going over how to configure their devices. I\u0027d prefer some naming that really explains the behavior like stayOnJustConnectedBadWifiIfNotPortal or preferBadWifiIfJustConnected or...",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 254,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "df5d20e0f167514b3a552260e8cf39de415d248f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ead27ec_e8c9ce0d",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/MultinetworkPolicyTracker.java",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 254,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T09:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is in contrast and in context with the \"avoid bad wifi\" setting. I think the behavior is complex and we are better off giving it a rather symbolic name than trying to describe it, because any description will be either wrong or 6-lines long. Case in point :\n• If you don\u0027t have the context, I don\u0027t think your suggestions are easier to understand. You still need to have \"avoid bad wifi\" off, which is a complex combination of mcc/mnc-dependent configs, a setting, and a per-network toggle ; most of the complexity is still hidden from the namings you suggest, and I think they may make things harder to grasp by suggesting that \"staying on just connected bad wifi if not portal\" is all there is to it.\n• Conversely, if you do have the context, then staying is really not the matter, nor is being just connected, and it becomes more confusing than the current naming too.\n• I think there is something to say for shorter names. The current name is already painful for its unwieldliness.",
      "parentUuid": "14b54f03_0e5743da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 254,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "df5d20e0f167514b3a552260e8cf39de415d248f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
